# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Yuanchang Zhou et al. (2026). Breaking the Training Barrier of Billion-Parameter Universal Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2604.15821  arXiv:2604.15821v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2604.15821v1 (sha256 9bc7c6a155fc494c...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 310 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zhou2026breaking.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: MatRIS-MoE (introduced here, extending MatRIS with
# mixture-of-experts layers) in three sizes, of which only the small model
# (1.09B parameters) is fully trained on a 473-million-configuration
# multi-domain data set; the medium and large models are used only for
# scaling studies. Accuracy is shown only as normalised scores (Fig. 5);
# the HPC performance figures are training-throughput measurements.

